  "placement": "Book page 38, topic 2.3: স্কেলার ও ভেক্টর রাশি. Next to চিত্র ২.০৩ (vectors A, B, C, D), or in place of it.",
  "order": 1,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "mm",
  "description": "Interactive 3D version of the book's চিত্র ২.০৩ (page 38, 2.3): four arrow pieces A, B, C, D lie on graph paper with a compass rose. Drag an arrow by its body to move it (its মান and দিক stay the same: the same vector), drag its head to turn it (দিক, in 15° steps from পূর্ব) or stretch it (মান, counted by the marks on it, one per unit), and drop it on another arrow's tail to compare: only when মান and দিক are both equal are they the same vector, wherever they were drawn. The panel reads the chosen arrow's মান and দিক and states the caption's verdicts; buttons line up the book's pairs A–B, A–C, C–D. Test tab: 5 questions (which arrow equals A, why two vectors differ, scalar or vector, what makes '4 km from home' a position, reading an arrow's মান and দিক). Phone-first, Bangla.",
  "tags": ["vector", "scalar", "magnitude", "direction", "motion", "bangla"],
  "params": [
